      "clin": "Cervicogenic dizziness (CGD)",
      "blurb": "A feeling of being off-balance or unsteady that may come from the neck. Your brain uses signals from the joints and muscles of the upper neck, together with your eyes and inner ear, to know where your head is. When the neck is sore, stiff or has been injured, those signals can become less accurate, and the brain may feel \"off\". It is not dangerous in itself, and it often eases as the neck settles and moves better. Because dizziness has several possible causes, these are checked first, so you get the right care; if your family doctor has not yet looked at your dizziness, see them alongside physiotherapy.",
