      "clin": "Myofascial pain syndrome: rhomboids, middle and lower trapezius, thoracic paraspinals",
      "blurb": "A muscle that has become tight and sensitive, often from being held in one position or worked harder than usual, can send a deep ache to a nearby area, such as from beside the spine to the edge of the shoulder blade. That spreading ache is a normal trick of the nervous system, not a trapped nerve or a damaged joint. A tender \"knot\" is not a tangle or a tear: it is a patch of muscle held tense to protect you, and it can be taught to let go again. It is common, not dangerous, and usually settles once the muscle is moved, loaded gradually, and the posture or habit that overloaded it is changed.",
